  "body": "Three cuts users expect that CamCraft cannot make:\n- Overlap: a closed cut returns exactly to its entry and leads out; the owner overlaps 1 mm (`Y-1.`) before the lead-out to remove the witness mark.\n- Slit on the wire centre line: a 0.3 mm slit (narrower than the 0.324 kerf) is refused (\"a corner of the open run near X-20.000 Y-11.850 is tighter than the wire can follow\"); there is no mode to cut a slit on the centre line at kerf width. Also: only the first violation is reported, and a whole-outline attempt reported an odd \"kerf would leave 6.0791 mm standing\".\n- Skims on open runs: \"an open run is cut once, from the air to its run-out\".\n\nDone means: each is an operation option with a test; defaults unchanged.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (#617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
